  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why the arrow points left",
      "items": [
        "Domain owns the interfaces; Infrastructure implements them",
        "The Web project's GlobalUsings expose only Dashboard.Domain.*",
        "Concrete infrastructure is named in Program.cs and nowhere else",
        "Domain carries no EF, no HTTP and no NetTopologySuite"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Every data feature is built this way",
      "items": [
        "Domain: records, a port, and a singleton state",
        "Infrastructure: typed client plus a background service on a timer",
        "Web: components subscribe and format through pure builders",
        "On failure MarkStale() keeps the last snapshot visible — a dead API never blanks a tile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Deliberately not in this diagram",
      "items": [
        "Asset proxies /tiles and /crests, on-disk cached with a host allowlist, keep the display off the internet",
        "The read-only research schema has its own ResearchDbContext and is excluded from migrations",
        "Analytics split into pure domain calculators and thin web builders"
      ]
    }
  ]
